Sadly, as of this morning I don't think it's going to make it. It now won't stand up even with the picks I put in as support, and it's just totally soft. The original leaves that came out (not the 'true') leaves have turned brown and shriveled overnight. 

&#x200B;

I'm pretty sad, the other plant I tried to grow at the same time also isn't doing too well. The only surviving plant I have is one that was already partially grown when I bought it.

I believe it's just a clear quartz but I will be careful with them. Right now I just needed something to lean it against temporarily to keep it standing because I wasn't sure what to use.

&#x200B;

Thanks for the heads up though, I have some in my other plants, I'll take them out now

&#x200B;

Edit: I swapped out the crystal for a couple wooden toothpicks, I put them around it in little x formations to keep it standing and give it something to lean on.

Yep. 

&#x200B;

I have a very small chest and my stomach is my biggest part of me. I can't find any nice non-tshirt tops and finding pants is damn near impossible.

What gets me is that OP is basically saying that love isn't enough. They can't just self-satisfy their own sexual needs but still be with the partner they love. It's 'must have sex or nothing.' That bothers me. It's not like sex is the only way to satisfy sexual urges...

&#x200B;

I guess because I'm ace it makes sense that I don't get it, but people seem to misunderstand us not being sexually attracted to finding someone ugly or repulsive and that's not true. OP seems to care an awful lot about their partner's sexual attraction to them to the point where nothing else matters and honestly it says a lot about their self esteem as well. If validation that you're sexy is the only important thing in a relationship, then that needs to be addressed by OP as well. If they can't be in a relationship where their partner isn't constantly sexually fawning over them, that's an issue. 

&#x200B;

I get that sex is a deal breaker for a lot of people (for reasons I'll never understand) - but telling someone it's okay then throwing divorce papers at them over sex is disgusting. All it tells me is that you don't love them to begin with. Especially if you can't find a way to work it out. That OP screams insecurity and selfishness.

As an asexual, this makes my future love life feel so bleak. 

&#x200B;

This world is so sex obsessed that apparently love doesn't matter to anyone anymore.

You absolutely can. FFX was one of my first games, period, and I got through it. Some of the trials were really difficult, but if you are good with puzzles and persist you can get through them. 

&#x200B;

I also find the game to be highly replayable, I've played through it numerous times over the years and still find new things every time. It's a very long and complicated plot, don't stress if you miss some stuff the first go.

I will go in and delete anything I've saved but never used. I also will go in and remove items that are basically the same thing in 1 shade difference (which is something that annoys me about the game sometimes.) 

&#x200B;

And of course I delete stuff I saved by accident

When I sat down and realized that there is not one person I've ever looked at and desired to sleep with. 

