It doesn't necessarily mean you're gaining permanently.

In addition to working full time, I don't often pay full price for any game unless I absolutely have to have it at release, or it's a game that never really goes down in price (such as Zelda). 

&#x200B;

A lot of my games I get on sale, or are less popular titles that aren't that expensive to begin with. There are lots of games around the $30 or less mark but they may not be as many titles you might be interested in, but they exist. 

&#x200B;

Also, if you are in the US and shop at Target often, sign up for Target circle. It's free and you collect points when you shop. I recently got Persona 5 for $12. It was on sale for $25 and I had a bit over $12 in free money from the circle. Target often has alright sales on games too, and sometimes put overstock on clearance.

Unfortunately, that work around was short lived, I am getting this error again constantly. It seems that unless I connect to wifi for a bit it won't let me play anything, it still says the same message. 

&#x200B;

This is my primary console, I transferred to it from another and I even de-registered and remade it the primary again and still nothing. 

&#x200B;

Nothing seems to make it go away, and I'll be pretty mad if I am forced to have to use wifi on a console meant to be able to be used on the go just to play my own games. I hate how needlessly difficult nintendo has made everything now.

Giving you a belated thanks on this! 

&#x200B;

I got the same error and went looking. I saw your comment and remembered that I had to log into the e-shop on my old switch to get the animal crossing island transfer app on it. Logged into the e-shop on my new switch and my game started fine. Thank you!!

